  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656100",
      "title": "Projecting Content into Components with ng-content",
      "lectureOrder": 400,
      "videoOrder": 369,
      "sourceHash": "fade0771916ab6c3f1880693d6a4b7694875c6aa85ed8bf0bbc25f35edcbb7f2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.552,
          "end": 5.34,
          "en": "-: So we learn a lot throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.34,
          "end": 7.32,
          "en": "We learned how to pass data around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.32,
          "end": 8.97,
          "en": "How to get access to elements in our dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 10.29,
          "en": "How to use local references.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.29,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "So our application now is much more dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 16.2,
          "en": "We got much more tools to interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.2,
          "end": 19.59,
          "en": "between the different pieces we have in our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.59,
          "end": 22.29,
          "en": "Now there is another way we can pass data around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "The last way for now in our server element component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "Right now we check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 32.81,
          "en": "if we have a type server or a type blueprint server, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.293,
          "end": 34.744,
          "en": "Nothing wrong with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.744,
          "end": 39.744,
          "en": "but sometimes you have complex HTML code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 44.258,
          "en": "which you want to pass into a component from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.258,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "So imagine you don't want to set this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 47.907,
          "en": "up inside the component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.907,
          "end": 51.213,
          "en": "I cut it instead in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.213,
          "end": 54.87,
          "en": "you some want to add this here between the opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.87,
          "end": 57.805,
          "en": "and closing element of your own component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.805,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "And there we simply would have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 62.67,
          "en": "to replace element with server element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.67,
          "end": 65.017,
          "en": "And we should expect us to work, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.017,
          "end": 67.29,
          "en": "So if we saved us and let it reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.29,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "and we add a new server, we don't get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 73.293,
          "en": "But the content is also not there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.293,
          "end": 75.593,
          "en": "and that is the default behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.593,
          "end": 78.78,
          "en": "Everything you place between the opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 83.07,
          "en": "and closing tag of your own component is lost by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "It's simply removed from the dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 88.951,
          "en": "Angler will not take care about it, but you can change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.951,
          "end": 91.658,
          "en": "There is a special directive and it is a directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.658,
          "end": 94.17,
          "en": "even though it looks like a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.17,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "but it doesn't have its own template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 97.869,
          "en": "A special directive you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.869,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "in these server element components template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 104.07,
          "en": "Here in the place where I want to render the content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.07,
          "end": 107.31,
          "en": "I can add NG content opening and closing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.31,
          "end": 109.539,
          "en": "Again, it still is a directive just using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.539,
          "end": 112.376,
          "en": "this element like selector, and this serves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.376,
          "end": 116.32300000000001,
          "en": "as a hook you can place in your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.32300000000001,
          "end": 119.245,
          "en": "to mark the place for Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.245,
          "end": 122.79,
          "en": "where it should add any content it finds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.79,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "between the opening and closing tag here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 129.93,
          "en": "So this content in this case with this tiny addition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.93,
          "end": 133.069,
          "en": "you should see that once you saved this and let it reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.069,
          "end": 134.89,
          "en": "If we add this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.073,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "and we click add server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 141.51,
          "en": "you now see the content is back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.51,
          "end": 144.21,
          "en": "It looks exactly the way it looked before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.21,
          "end": 147.03,
          "en": "but technically something totally different works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.03,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "or happens here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 152.4,
          "en": "Now we add this via the NG content hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.4,
          "end": 154.68,
          "en": "We add it between the opening and closing tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 158.57999999999998,
          "en": "and therefore it will be projected into your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.57999999999998,
          "end": 161.817,
          "en": "projected into your server element component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.817,
          "end": 163.524,
          "en": "A nice feature, especially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.524,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "if you think about building reusable widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 169.92000000000002,
          "en": "like a tab widget where each tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.92000000000002,
          "end": 171.87,
          "en": "will have a content which probably comes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.87,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "from some other source and which you don't want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "to pass through property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 178.86,
          "en": "which always would be an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.86,
          "end": 181.273,
          "en": "But if it's more complex HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.273,
          "end": 184.17,
          "en": "property binding really is not the best solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.17,
          "end": 186.756,
          "en": "because Angular will escape HTML texts there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.756,
          "end": 189.78,
          "en": "to prevent cross sites scripting attacks from happening.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 189.78,
          "end": 191.94,
          "en": "And you could kind of work around that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.94,
          "end": 194.25,
          "en": "But really energy content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "that is how you want to display this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 199.803,
          "en": "and that is a great tool to have at your disposal.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
